{"files":[{"content":"/*\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\n\n    The stencil calculation stops when  ( err >= CONV_THRESHOLD OR  iter > ITER_MAX )\n*/\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <time.h>\n#include <sys/time.h>\n\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f // threshold of convergence\n\n// matrix to be solved\ndouble **grid;\n\n// auxiliary matrix\ndouble **new_grid;\n\n// size of each side of the grid\nint size;\nint iter_max_num;\n\n// return the absolute value of a number\ndouble absolute(double num){\n    if(num < 0)\n        return -1.0 * num;\n    return num;\n}\n\n\n// allocate memory for the grid\nvoid allocate_memory(){\n    grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\n    new_grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\n\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\n        new_grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\n    }\n}\n\n// initialize the grid\nvoid initialize_grid(){\n    int center = size / 2;\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            // inicializa região de calor no centro do grid\n            if ( i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup)\n                grid[i][j] = 100;\n            else\n                grid[i][j] = 0;\n            // Both buffers retain the same fixed boundary values when their roles swap.\n            new_grid[i][j] = grid[i][j];\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// save the grid in a file\nvoid save_grid(){\n\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            fprintf(stdout, \"%lf \", grid[i][j]);\n        }\n        fprintf(stdout, \"\\n\");\n    }\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]){\n\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &size);\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &iter_max_num);\n    \n    int hasError = 1;\n    double max_error = 0.0;\n\n    struct timeval time_start;\n    struct timeval time_end;\n\n    // allocate memory to the grid (matrix)\n    allocate_memory();\n\n    // set grid initial conditions\n    initialize_grid();\n\n    //printf(\"Jacobi relaxation calculation: %d x %d grid\\n\", size, size);\n\n    // get the start time\n    //gettimeofday(&time_start, NULL);\n\n    // Keep one team alive across iterations. Every thread follows the same\n    // bounded loop and observes the convergence decision after the single barrier.\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        for (int iter = 0; iter < iter_max_num; iter++) {\n\n            #pragma omp single\n            {\n                max_error = 0.0;\n            }\n\n            // Assign contiguous complete rows to each thread. The max reduction\n            // records the largest cell change for the shared convergence test.\n            #pragma omp for schedule(static) reduction(max:max_error)\n            for (int i = 1; i < size-1; i++) {\n                for (int j = 1; j < size-1; j++) {\n                    new_grid[i][j] = 0.25 * (grid[i][j+1] + grid[i][j-1] +\n                                             grid[i-1][j] + grid[i+1][j]);\n\n                    double errorCurrent = absolute(new_grid[i][j] - grid[i][j]);\n                    if (errorCurrent > max_error) {\n                        max_error = errorCurrent;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            // Swap only after every interior cell is ready, then stop all\n            // threads together if the strict convergence threshold is met.\n            #pragma omp single\n            {\n                hasError = max_error > CONV_THRESHOLD;\n                double **temporary_grid = grid;\n                grid = new_grid;\n                new_grid = temporary_grid;\n            }\n\n            if (!hasError) {\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // get the end time\n    //gettimeofday(&time_end, NULL);\n\n    //double exec_time = (double) (time_end.tv_sec - time_start.tv_sec) +\n    //                   (double) (time_end.tv_usec - time_start.tv_usec) / 1000000.0;\n\n    //save the final grid in file\n    save_grid();\n\n    //printf(\"\\nKernel executed in %lf seconds with %d iterations.\\n\", exec_time, iter);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/laplace_seq.c"}],"hypothesis":"On the four-core ARM target, assigning contiguous complete rows with schedule(static) instead of collapsing both dimensions may reduce work-distribution overhead and retain row locality. A bounded per-thread iteration loop keeps the persistent team's convergence and barrier decisions uniform.","notes":"This is a performance hypothesis, not a measured result. The row stencil arithmetic, update buffer swap, strict convergence comparison, iteration limit, and output formatting are preserved.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace collapsed two-dimensional work sharing with static work sharing over complete rows.","Use a bounded iteration loop in the persistent parallel region and make the convergence decision and buffer swap in a single region before threads uniformly exit." ]}